WEBVTT

00:21.510 --> 00:23.740
Immortal, my butt!

00:23.740 --> 00:26.210
You're just a bloodthirsty monster!

00:48.970 --> 00:51.360
<i>Done playing around?</i>

00:54.080 --> 00:55.700
S-Stop, it's me!

00:56.640 --> 00:58.660
Oh, it's you, Fujikuro.

00:58.970 --> 01:01.120
Watch who you're fighting!

01:02.600 --> 01:04.580
<i>— Good job, Iria.</i>
— Thanks!

01:04.950 --> 01:07.170
Good job?

01:08.410 --> 01:10.880
What am I supposed to do with you two?

01:11.240 --> 01:15.930
Zeiram this, Zeiram that, can't
you two think of something else?

01:15.930 --> 01:17.840
<i>You’ll understand once you meet him.</i>

01:18.140 --> 01:20.930
You almost killed me.

01:20.930 --> 01:22.810
I should have followed through.

01:22.810 --> 01:23.750
What?

01:23.750 --> 01:26.720
Just a bit further and I would've killed him...

01:26.720 --> 01:27.810
Oh well...

01:28.120 --> 01:33.280
What the hell? I brought flowers for your birthday!

01:36.970 --> 01:39.650
<i>You’re trying too hard, Fujikuro.</i>

01:39.650 --> 01:42.200
I'm not trying anything.

01:43.140 --> 01:46.160
<i>Here we go. It’s the message you’ve been waiting for.</i>

01:46.650 --> 01:47.750
It's here?

01:48.010 --> 01:50.060
<i>Congratulations!</i>

01:50.060 --> 01:53.210
<i>Your licence number is 9799-5.</i>

01:53.930 --> 01:55.530
Congratulations!

01:55.530 --> 01:57.610
Now, you're a fully
licensed, legit Hunter!

01:57.610 --> 01:58.710
Yes!

01:59.270 --> 02:01.700
Why don't you hop in my new ride.

02:01.700 --> 02:04.150
I'll give you a lift to the office.

02:25.910 --> 02:33.280
<i>The night sky has betrayed the stars...</i>

02:36.420 --> 02:43.930
<i>A faraway cry slowly fades.</i>

02:46.890 --> 02:57.250
<i>The sun has disappeared...</i>

02:57.250 --> 03:07.410
<i>and my heart is alone
with the revelation.</i>

03:10.340 --> 03:18.490
<i>A stranger's dreams appear.</i>

03:20.970 --> 03:29.230
<i>Tempting lost souls.</i>

03:31.390 --> 03:39.350
<i>A stranger's dreams appear.</i>

03:37.400 --> 03:41.300
Iria: Zeiram the Animation

03:41.300 --> 03:45.000
Broom Tree

03:54.140 --> 03:57.790
<i>We are asking all occupants to
evacuate, due to redevelopment.</i>

03:57.790 --> 04:00.850
<i>We cannot guarantee the safety
of non compliant residents.</i>

04:00.850 --> 04:05.090
<i>We are asking all occupants to
evacuate, due to redevelopment...</i>

04:05.750 --> 04:07.500
What are you doing, Sara?

04:08.220 --> 04:10.770
— Where are Kei and Komimasa?
— How should I know!

04:15.760 --> 04:18.140
They're tearing this place down!

04:18.140 --> 04:20.750
I'm sick of this, dammit!

04:20.750 --> 04:22.570
— Let's leave!
— Leave?

04:22.780 --> 04:23.910
Let's go to Myce!

04:25.360 --> 04:27.910
If we find your brother,
we'll be okay, right?

04:28.000 --> 04:29.480
— My brother?
— Yeah.

04:29.480 --> 04:31.370
Hey, slow down!

04:42.520 --> 04:45.280
— What do you think?
— Looks like it's leaving.

04:45.280 --> 04:47.510
— Cool, let's go!
— Yeah!

04:52.890 --> 04:53.770
Found it!

04:54.000 --> 04:55.850
Kei, hop in!

04:56.400 --> 04:58.400
Really?

04:58.700 --> 05:01.360
We have a famous scientist
like that on Taowajan?

05:03.580 --> 05:05.510
We made it!

05:05.510 --> 05:07.820
When we wake up, we'll be in Myce.

05:07.900 --> 05:10.790
That monster showed up on Myce too, huh?

05:10.960 --> 05:12.130
Who knows.

05:12.130 --> 05:15.300
That's why he was called out.
He's supposed to be the expert.

05:15.300 --> 05:19.180
Expert? I heard he was a
retired, grouchy bastard!

05:19.180 --> 05:20.040
Shut up!

05:20.070 --> 05:22.840
I'm Dr. Touka! This is it, right?

05:22.970 --> 05:25.010
O-Oh, Dr. Touka!

05:25.010 --> 05:28.540
Sir, we've been waiting for you.

05:28.540 --> 05:29.850
Let me get your bags.

05:29.850 --> 05:30.950
I can get it myself!

05:30.950 --> 05:33.180
Yes, sir! Of course!

05:33.180 --> 05:36.020
— Just get me on board.
— Y-Yes, sir!

05:36.040 --> 05:38.860
Have a safe trip, sir.

05:40.010 --> 05:43.710
Don't mind an old geezer like me. Thank you.

05:47.950 --> 05:49.160
Who are you?

05:50.960 --> 05:53.480
Sorry, but we're taking this ship.

05:53.480 --> 05:55.000
You're coming with us, grandpa!

05:55.240 --> 05:56.460
Don't hurt him!

05:57.160 --> 06:00.100
We won't, he looks important.

06:00.100 --> 06:03.420
You want money? Nobody's gonna pay for
an old bastard like me!

06:03.420 --> 06:04.300
Stop it!

06:04.840 --> 06:09.060
If we run into trouble,
I'll use this baby!

06:09.060 --> 06:11.440
— You've got yours, right?
— Um, yeah...

06:12.760 --> 06:14.620
But I'm out of stones.

06:14.620 --> 06:17.410
What are you good for?

06:17.410 --> 06:20.980
Fine. Don't worry, I'll take care of you.

06:21.380 --> 06:23.940
Man, I'm getting excited!

06:27.230 --> 06:28.910
We have to report this!

06:34.750 --> 06:37.550
How long do we have to wait?

06:37.550 --> 06:39.410
This is why I don't like bureaucracy.

06:39.410 --> 06:42.840
— Things seem a bit weird today.
— I suppose.

06:47.910 --> 06:51.680
Registration number 9799-5, Iria.

06:51.870 --> 06:53.010
Yes.

06:54.490 --> 06:56.970
— Please confirm.
— Yes, sir!

06:57.520 --> 06:58.940
It's perfect.

06:59.020 --> 07:00.890
I wish you the best of luck.

07:00.890 --> 07:02.310
Thank you.

07:06.280 --> 07:09.420
It looks like something big's going down.

07:09.420 --> 07:11.490
<i>— Iria.</i>
— Bob?

07:11.990 --> 07:15.200
<i>— Take me to the access terminal.</i>
— Okay.

07:22.500 --> 07:24.570
He's useful, isn't he?

07:24.570 --> 07:26.750
You could be too, if you
had an accident like Bob did.

07:26.750 --> 07:27.960
No thanks.

07:28.610 --> 07:30.130
Find anything?

07:30.350 --> 07:33.090
<i>Looks big, however...</i>

07:33.300 --> 07:36.570
— Dr. Touka was abducted?
<i>— Correct.</i>

07:36.570 --> 07:38.870
A rescue team is on their way, right?

07:38.870 --> 07:40.560
<i>— They’ve been wiped out.</i>
— What?

07:40.910 --> 07:42.600
<i>They were murdered.</i>

07:42.600 --> 07:46.270
Wait a sec. When did this happen?

07:46.460 --> 07:50.400
<i>Just now. They didn’t last an hour.</i>

07:50.400 --> 07:53.210
<i>They sent ten men, but
they’ve lost all contact.</i>

07:53.210 --> 07:56.590
— You're not gonna give Iria this job, are you?
<i>— Correct.</i>

07:56.590 --> 07:58.890
Wait, this is her first case!

07:58.890 --> 08:01.680
— I'll be fine.
— No, you won't!

08:01.680 --> 08:03.460
I have a bad feeling about this.

08:03.460 --> 08:05.330
I'm always right about this kind of stuff.

08:05.330 --> 08:07.580
Don't get involved in this one.

08:07.580 --> 08:08.540
<i>It pays well.</i>

08:08.540 --> 08:12.150
Money doesn't mean
anything if you're dead!

08:12.150 --> 08:13.720
Ten guys are dead already!

08:14.000 --> 08:16.180
<i>I’m not asking you.</i>

08:16.210 --> 08:19.110
You're still hard-headed,
you haven't changed!

08:19.110 --> 08:20.270
Fujikuro.

08:20.300 --> 08:21.930
What's wrong?

08:22.450 --> 08:25.950
I can see right through the bastard.

08:25.950 --> 08:27.820
<i>Just stay out of it.</i>

08:27.820 --> 08:29.430
You liar!

08:29.430 --> 08:31.800
This isn't about money!

08:31.800 --> 08:34.170
You just want to meet Dr. Touka!

08:34.170 --> 08:36.410
<i>It’s a rescue mission.</i>

08:36.410 --> 08:38.180
Slow down!

08:38.180 --> 08:42.370
You're losing me. Who is this Dr. Touka?

08:42.680 --> 08:46.110
Dr. Touka is the number one
expert on Zeiram research...

08:46.110 --> 08:48.340
Well, so I've heard...

08:50.270 --> 08:51.900
Is that true, Bob?

08:51.900 --> 08:55.300
<i>He’s the only surviving researcher.</i>

08:55.300 --> 08:57.550
Now hold on!

08:57.550 --> 09:00.830
You both get crazy when you
hear Zeiram's name mentioned.

09:00.830 --> 09:03.540
Do you think the kidnappers
are connected to Zeiram?

09:03.540 --> 09:04.640
Listen to me!

09:04.640 --> 09:05.930
<i>I doubt it.</i>

09:05.930 --> 09:08.300
<i>Iria, listen to my plan.</i>

09:08.300 --> 09:10.980
If I find him, I can ask
him about Zeiram, right?

09:10.980 --> 09:12.230
<i>— Probably.</i>
— Guys!

09:12.230 --> 09:13.360
Okay.

09:13.360 --> 09:15.470
Fujikuro, I need you to give me a ride.

09:15.470 --> 09:17.650
Wait, hold on...

09:17.650 --> 09:20.370
I told you, I'm not
your personal chauffeur!

09:53.530 --> 09:54.610
What's that?

09:54.740 --> 09:57.570
That was me. I'm starving!

09:59.000 --> 10:00.830
Me too.

10:02.410 --> 10:05.520
Hey, don't get depressed!

10:05.520 --> 10:07.860
We're on Myce.

10:07.860 --> 10:10.440
That ruckus back there was unexpected...

10:10.440 --> 10:11.230
Yeah.

10:11.230 --> 10:14.430
C'mon, cheer up. Maybe we'll find Iria.

10:14.430 --> 10:16.130
Huh, what are you talking about?

10:16.130 --> 10:18.880
She's got nothing to do with this!

10:23.830 --> 10:26.930
Hey, I have to tell you something.

10:27.310 --> 10:29.900
It looks like we hit the jackpot!

10:33.310 --> 10:35.820
Komimasa, are you okay?

10:36.380 --> 10:38.050
I'm fine.

10:38.050 --> 10:40.990
Take a look, it's a cafeteria!

10:40.990 --> 10:43.070
Food, food!

10:47.750 --> 10:49.710
Kei, help look around for stuff!

10:55.190 --> 10:57.240
I found a new bag.

10:57.240 --> 10:58.800
Does it have food in it?

11:04.100 --> 11:06.190
What is this?

11:06.610 --> 11:09.890
"An Analysis of the Zeiram Unit"...

11:10.840 --> 11:13.020
It's all dried up.

11:13.020 --> 11:14.360
Can we sell that for a good price?

11:14.620 --> 11:17.280
It's not worth the effort.

11:17.280 --> 11:21.160
We're finally on Myce, but
we're still starving and broke.

11:21.160 --> 11:23.140
This just sucks!

11:23.140 --> 11:24.870
Hey, listen to me.

11:24.870 --> 11:27.500
I really don't have a brother.

11:27.500 --> 11:30.330
— I don't know anybody in Myce.
— Really?

11:30.610 --> 11:33.910
I never thought this would happen.

11:33.910 --> 11:35.810
I'm sorry about lying to you.

11:35.810 --> 11:37.300
I know what's up.

11:37.640 --> 11:40.350
You'd be embarrassed if I met your bro.

11:40.350 --> 11:43.760
It's all right, I'll behave, okay?

11:46.010 --> 11:48.640
<i>First, we’ll teleport in the sensors.</i>

11:48.650 --> 11:50.270
<i>What if they spot the transmission?</i>

11:50.280 --> 11:52.430
<i>Timing will be critical.</i>

11:52.430 --> 11:54.650
<i>Feel things out with the sensor.</i>

11:54.650 --> 11:57.940
<i>The gate will be open for five
seconds, so start shooting.</i>

11:58.320 --> 12:01.530
<i>Once they’re down,
move in with the Kreper.</i>

12:01.780 --> 12:03.360
<i>I suggest using type two weapons.</i>

12:04.730 --> 12:05.620
Roger!

12:11.730 --> 12:12.520
Ready!

12:21.970 --> 12:23.860
I see three of them!

12:23.860 --> 12:26.550
Unbelievable, they haven't
noticed the teleport.

12:26.690 --> 12:27.930
<i>I’m opening the door.</i>

12:27.930 --> 12:29.140
Go for it!

12:40.460 --> 12:42.030
<i>What’s going on?</i>

12:43.220 --> 12:44.550
My brother...

12:44.550 --> 12:46.020
<i>What?</i>

12:46.410 --> 12:48.760
I saw Glen in there!

12:48.760 --> 12:49.740
<i>Are you sure?</i>

12:51.810 --> 12:55.370
<i>We’re booked for three
transits, it’s your call.</i>

12:55.670 --> 12:57.880
I'm going in!

13:12.640 --> 13:13.890
Let's go!

13:16.240 --> 13:18.250
He's dead.

13:18.250 --> 13:21.070
Let's take his money and run!

13:22.070 --> 13:24.430
— It's heavy.
— Cool!

13:24.680 --> 13:26.650
Achoo!

13:26.650 --> 13:29.160
What are you two doing here?

13:29.690 --> 13:31.930
You scared me! I thought you were dead!

13:31.930 --> 13:33.660
Hurry up and untie me!

13:33.660 --> 13:36.200
No need to order us around, grandpa!

13:36.200 --> 13:41.130
Yeah, you need to give us a reward
for saving you, like food or cash.

13:41.370 --> 13:43.590
You already took my money.

13:43.810 --> 13:46.880
We found this before you woke up!

13:46.880 --> 13:51.850
We might as well have found
it on the street, it's ours.

13:52.250 --> 13:54.220
Yeah, that's right!

13:55.130 --> 13:58.560
If you don't have anything
else, I guess we'll have to...

13:58.650 --> 14:03.360
You numbskulls! Stop wasting my time and untie me!

14:06.290 --> 14:08.320
We're not giving your wallet back.

14:09.070 --> 14:11.580
What is this, he's
not one of our targets...

14:11.960 --> 14:13.910
<i>Let me take a look.</i>

14:18.160 --> 14:21.000
<i>I’ve never seen anything like these in the Myce
system.</i>

14:21.300 --> 14:24.040
This is getting complicated.

14:24.040 --> 14:26.120
What's going on with Glen?

14:32.110 --> 14:33.970
This is the fifth one.

14:34.650 --> 14:36.680
The suspects are all dead.

14:37.120 --> 14:40.650
<i>They all have their chests
torn open with the same weapon.</i>

14:40.760 --> 14:42.700
A bag? A red bag?

14:42.700 --> 14:44.570
That's right, where did you see it?

14:44.570 --> 14:45.800
How much will you give us for it?

14:45.800 --> 14:48.840
Is that all you have on
your mind, you little punks?

14:48.840 --> 14:52.070
— Food works, too.
— It's important, right?

14:52.220 --> 14:54.030
We need a reward.

14:54.040 --> 14:56.990
Never mind, I'll look for it myself!

14:57.870 --> 15:00.170
You win, old geezer!

15:04.120 --> 15:06.260
This is the rescue team!

15:06.610 --> 15:08.790
<i>This is really bad...</i>

15:08.790 --> 15:12.390
<i>This is the work of a crazy lunatic,
or there’s more behind this...</i>

15:12.740 --> 15:15.010
No doubt!

15:26.000 --> 15:28.650
Not the brightest way to escape!

15:29.240 --> 15:31.610
Dear God! I'm getting a signal!

15:31.890 --> 15:34.650
— What is that?
— A Zeiram sensor.

15:34.650 --> 15:36.220
What's a Zeiram?

15:36.220 --> 15:40.590
It was the monster that caused a
ruckus on Taowajan the other day.

15:40.590 --> 15:42.890
What? He's around here somewhere?

15:42.890 --> 15:44.590
You know about Zeiram?

15:44.590 --> 15:48.340
Of course we know,
we're from Taowajan.

15:48.530 --> 15:55.300
I see, you're one of the local street urchins. That explains it!

15:55.500 --> 15:58.910
How can you be so calm, we're
gonna be toast if he's here!

15:58.910 --> 16:00.520
Do you have any weapons?

16:00.790 --> 16:02.840
No weapons.

16:02.840 --> 16:04.230
The signal's getting stronger.

16:04.540 --> 16:06.190
He's getting closer!

16:11.740 --> 16:14.110
It looks different this time!

16:14.110 --> 16:15.460
Komimasa!

16:15.460 --> 16:18.330
This can't be Zeiram, something's wrong.

16:27.990 --> 16:28.880
Iria!

16:29.290 --> 16:32.220
He tore everybody
apart with these claws.

16:37.070 --> 16:38.670
Iria!

16:38.670 --> 16:41.310
What are you doing here?

16:41.460 --> 16:44.140
Phew, that was close!

16:44.430 --> 16:47.000
The sensor's still picking up a signal...

16:47.980 --> 16:49.690
You must be Dr. Touka!

16:49.970 --> 16:51.790
It's an honour to meet you.

16:51.790 --> 16:54.150
I'm Iria, a Hunter, I'm here to rescue you.

16:54.430 --> 16:57.120
Finally. You took your time.

16:58.220 --> 16:59.670
I apologise.

16:59.670 --> 17:02.500
Ignore him, he's a rude bastard.

17:02.640 --> 17:05.450
Shut up! You two have no right to talk!

17:05.450 --> 17:06.920
I do appreciate your coming, though.

17:08.300 --> 17:09.880
Are you guys okay?

17:10.150 --> 17:11.580
Of course!

17:11.580 --> 17:13.590
You were worried about us?

17:13.860 --> 17:15.580
Think what you want.

17:15.580 --> 17:17.800
I forgot that you were so tough.

17:17.890 --> 17:21.140
Don't be so cold, Kei missed you a lot.

17:21.190 --> 17:23.260
Shut up, Komimasa!

17:23.260 --> 17:27.900
He wanted to see you, so he said
that he had a brother working on Myce.

17:27.900 --> 17:30.000
I'd know if he had a brother by now!

17:30.000 --> 17:32.710
It was pretty obvious, he can
be such a kid sometimes.

17:32.710 --> 17:34.360
You're both still kids.

17:34.730 --> 17:37.270
I was going to ask you
to return my hair beads.

17:37.270 --> 17:39.320
Oh well, keep them.

17:39.700 --> 17:42.910
We should keep moving.

17:42.910 --> 17:45.790
We picked up two Zeiram signals earlier.

17:46.060 --> 17:47.930
What did you say?

17:52.300 --> 17:53.170
Glen!

17:54.140 --> 17:55.550
That's your brother?

18:01.550 --> 18:02.970
Now, run!

18:05.060 --> 18:07.060
Iria, hurry!

18:10.030 --> 18:11.060
Iria!

18:13.980 --> 18:15.010
Kei!

18:15.010 --> 18:16.990
— Don't just stand there, Iria!
— I'm sorry!

18:17.410 --> 18:20.950
Iria...

18:26.010 --> 18:28.500
Thanks for saving me.

18:28.880 --> 18:30.490
Again...

18:30.490 --> 18:32.090
I'm hungry!

18:32.090 --> 18:34.880
You can thank me with food and cash!

18:35.130 --> 18:36.590
You haven't changed.

18:36.700 --> 18:39.390
That was my last bullet.

18:39.390 --> 18:40.550
Hey, Iria?

18:40.670 --> 18:41.390
Yes?

18:41.650 --> 18:44.240
Your brother... It was his pendant?

18:44.240 --> 18:46.670
Yes, he's my partner.

18:46.670 --> 18:48.140
<i>Dr. Touka!</i>

18:48.140 --> 18:49.980
<i>What the hell were those monsters?</i>

18:49.980 --> 18:51.270
What is that?

18:51.550 --> 18:52.880
Meet Bob, my other partner.

18:52.880 --> 18:54.570
<i>Greetings, Kei and Komimasa.</i>

18:54.980 --> 18:57.030
— Oh, hi...
— What a weirdo!

18:58.840 --> 19:01.910
It's faint, but we're receiving
signals from the Zeiram Sensor.

19:02.170 --> 19:04.490
But that wasn't a Zeiram, right?

19:04.490 --> 19:07.200
As far as I know.

19:07.200 --> 19:10.070
It's possible that Zeiram
has created genetic clones.

19:10.070 --> 19:12.630
So that was a clone of my brother?

19:12.920 --> 19:16.420
I'm not sure. It's still just a theory.

19:16.470 --> 19:21.130
If that's the case, did he kill my
brother and assimilate his cells?

19:21.500 --> 19:24.010
Do I have to repeat myself?

19:24.010 --> 19:27.350
I can't say until I
see it with my own eyes!

19:29.310 --> 19:34.270
But as far as I know, you
can't generate clones from dead cells.

19:34.270 --> 19:38.390
That's enough of that subject,
we should plan our next move.

19:38.390 --> 19:39.490
So, what do we do?

19:39.920 --> 19:42.280
Use the teleporter and get out.

19:43.560 --> 19:46.160
That doesn't sound good, let's go!

19:54.130 --> 19:55.310
What's up?

19:55.310 --> 19:58.190
Bad news, the balancer's shot.

19:58.190 --> 20:00.550
Be careful, he might still be around.

20:00.910 --> 20:03.150
<i>The teleporter’s damaged as well.</i>

20:03.150 --> 20:05.690
It's almost like he's anticipating our moves.

20:05.690 --> 20:08.520
Doctor, can clones be that intelligent?

20:08.800 --> 20:10.530
I don't know.

20:10.530 --> 20:14.840
Look, they might not even be clones,
don't jump to conclusions.

20:15.620 --> 20:17.940
Iria, I can fix this!

20:18.130 --> 20:21.420
<i>That’s great! You’re smarter than Iria.</i>

20:21.420 --> 20:22.400
Leave me alone.

20:23.320 --> 20:25.700
We'll take care of you.

20:25.700 --> 20:26.660
Again!

20:26.660 --> 20:28.120
He's coming!

20:28.110 --> 20:29.340
Over there!

20:29.340 --> 20:32.250
Iria...

20:40.380 --> 20:42.130
Glen, is that you?

20:42.320 --> 20:43.890
Iria, no!

20:43.890 --> 20:46.340
He's a clone, he only
looks like your brother!

20:46.560 --> 20:49.260
Iria...

20:50.510 --> 20:52.020
He's not your brother!

20:52.390 --> 20:55.370
Kei, Komimasa, you two
watch the doctor, okay?

20:55.370 --> 20:56.730
What are you gonna do?

20:56.730 --> 20:59.170
I have to make sure with my own eyes.

20:59.170 --> 21:02.490
I'm warning you, we're not cheap labour.

21:09.140 --> 21:12.580
Iria...

21:14.380 --> 21:15.790
Glen?

21:21.970 --> 21:23.590
<i>Iria!</i>

21:25.790 --> 21:28.600
Grandpa, you gotta just trust us.

21:28.600 --> 21:30.810
We're doing this
because she asked us to.

21:30.810 --> 21:31.970
We've got a problem, Komimasa.

21:32.310 --> 21:33.930
There's no way outta here!

21:34.680 --> 21:37.400
How about that hole in the ceiling?

21:37.680 --> 21:40.220
We don't have enough power for that.

21:40.220 --> 21:42.110
Never mind.

21:43.210 --> 21:44.950
Hold it...

21:44.950 --> 21:46.450
I think this might help us out.

21:46.590 --> 21:47.910
Huh?

21:53.820 --> 21:55.660
<i>Iria, don’t hold back!</i>

21:55.660 --> 21:57.250
I know, but...

21:57.500 --> 22:00.420
Iria...

22:00.690 --> 22:02.630
Kei, keep your head down!

22:02.840 --> 22:05.090
No, Komimasa, that's the wrong way!

22:05.350 --> 22:06.680
Wrong what?

22:13.670 --> 22:15.780
<i>Iria, he’s just a clone.</i>

22:15.780 --> 22:17.190
We don't know that!

22:19.140 --> 22:20.730
Even if he is a clone,

22:22.480 --> 22:27.070
this ugly beast
looks nothing like Glen.

22:30.360 --> 22:32.240
But I can't be sure...

22:34.690 --> 22:37.110
<i>Glen would never attack you!</i>

22:37.110 --> 22:38.610
I don't know what to do!

22:38.610 --> 22:41.880
He's almost as strong
as my brother, for one thing.

22:43.800 --> 22:45.380
<i>Hold out your arm!</i>

22:58.480 --> 22:59.630
<i>Are you okay?</i>

22:59.630 --> 23:00.770
Yeah.

23:00.770 --> 23:01.940
<i>Iria, let me just say this.</i>

23:02.850 --> 23:06.400
<i>If this was really Glen,
you’d be dead by now.</i>

23:06.760 --> 23:07.700
I know.

23:07.700 --> 23:10.190
<i>Either way, let’s take a cell sample.</i>

23:10.190 --> 23:10.860
Okay.

23:12.730 --> 23:14.610
Iria, are you hurt?

23:14.610 --> 23:15.880
I'm fine.

23:15.880 --> 23:17.620
Any sign of Zeiram, Doctor?

23:18.280 --> 23:21.580
A very faint signal
is coming from close by.

23:21.610 --> 23:23.290
— Let's go!
— Okay!

23:32.520 --> 23:33.850
Hurry!

23:34.060 --> 23:35.310
I know!

23:39.620 --> 23:41.810
We made it!

23:45.360 --> 23:48.940
Gramps, can't you look happier?

23:48.940 --> 23:50.780
We're on Myce!

23:50.780 --> 23:54.550
And is that's supposed
to mean something to me?

23:54.550 --> 23:58.120
You don't get it, it
means something to us...

23:58.120 --> 24:00.120
That we're on Myce.

24:00.120 --> 24:02.170
Darn it, never mind!

24:02.510 --> 24:06.130
We don't have enough fuel
to make it over the hill!

24:06.400 --> 24:08.090
Don't worry, there's a lift nearby.

24:12.990 --> 24:15.760
Iria...

24:23.170 --> 24:24.250
It's that thing!

24:24.250 --> 24:25.190
It's still alive!

24:25.280 --> 24:27.650
Iria...

24:30.610 --> 24:31.900
Emergency, Iria!

24:32.170 --> 24:33.820
— He's back!
— What?

24:33.820 --> 24:35.330
Hurry!

24:36.430 --> 24:37.280
We did it!

24:44.360 --> 24:45.540
This is our chance!

24:45.770 --> 24:46.630
Move it!

24:46.630 --> 24:48.000
Hurry, grandpa!

24:48.580 --> 24:51.460
Iria...

25:04.140 --> 25:05.350
Komimasa!

25:17.860 --> 25:19.870
I wanted you to have this.

25:19.870 --> 25:22.250
I'm a lousy shot.

25:38.660 --> 25:40.970
I don't know you.

25:50.620 --> 25:52.690
Kei...

25:53.450 --> 26:00.480
We made lots of noise, and
we had a lot of fun, huh...

26:06.000 --> 26:07.040
Komimasa!

26:34.770 --> 26:37.920
Starting with this, I'll
have to revise my research.

26:39.270 --> 26:42.740
It reminds me of Komimasa...

26:43.060 --> 26:45.490
I'm also starving.

26:45.490 --> 26:47.710
We'll have dinner in
Komimasa's memory, okay?

26:47.870 --> 26:49.300
Yeah.

26:57.420 --> 27:02.670
<i>The morning to come
does not matter...</i>

27:02.670 --> 27:15.930
<i>let's go as we are now.</i>

27:15.930 --> 27:22.220
<i>We're passing a blue star...</i>

27:22.220 --> 27:28.350
<i>a tiny floating light.</i>

27:28.350 --> 27:34.740
<i>It's just the two
of us, no need to speak.</i>

27:34.740 --> 27:40.390
<i>Looking out over the city...</i>

27:40.390 --> 27:46.780
<i>The painful memories we have shared...</i>

27:46.780 --> 27:52.050
<i>they will be put to rest tonight.</i>

27:52.050 --> 27:58.630
<i>And the night to come
does not matter...</i>

27:58.630 --> 28:05.800
<i>let's go without looking back.</i>

28:05.800 --> 28:11.070
<i>Even though our dreams are far away...</i>

28:11.070 --> 28:18.630
<i>I will never let them go.</i>

28:33.850 --> 28:36.520
A scream pierces the
silence of the night...

28:37.940 --> 28:41.360
The cry tortures Iria's
trembling heart...

28:41.710 --> 28:45.000
Is it crying for salvation?

28:45.000 --> 28:47.050
Or is it a song of the damned?

28:47.990 --> 28:50.500
The scream echoes
through the night sky...

28:50.500 --> 28:53.330
The winds of death
blow through the city.

28:53.330 --> 28:56.000
No, I <i>will</i> save you!

28:56.000 --> 29:01.210
Wind Song.
